{
  "method": "exact recording script punctuation + prior transcript-constrained timing; terminology grouped together, not independent ASR",
  "protected_terms": [
    "van der Waals",
    "digital hyperextension",
    "Tokay gecko's"
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0.26,
      "end": 1.95,
      "text": "A gecko can hold onto a"
    },
    {
      "start": 1.95,
      "end": 2.54,
      "text": "wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.94,
      "end": 4.23,
      "text": "So how does it let go"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.23,
      "end": 5.19,
      "text": "with every step?"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.71,
      "end": 7.6,
      "text": "The secret isn't just a strong"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.6,
      "end": 8.12,
      "text": "grip."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.46,
      "end": 10.46,
      "text": "It's how that grip is controlled."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.08,
      "end": 12.78,
      "text": "Under a Tokay gecko's toes are"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.78,
      "end": 15.4,
      "text": "tiny, hair like structures called setae."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.14,
      "end": 18.57,
      "text": "Their branching tips make extremely close"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.57,
      "end": 19.79,
      "text": "contact with the surface."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.27,
      "end": 21.37,
      "text": "They aren't suction cups."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.79,
      "end": 23.16,
      "text": "At that tiny scale,"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.4,
      "end": 25.15,
      "text": "van der Waals forces help those"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.15,
      "end": 26.03,
      "text": "tips adhere."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.59,
      "end": 27.91,
      "text": "But direction matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.41,
      "end": 29.92,
      "text": "A pull toward the base of"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.92,
      "end": 32.0,
      "text": "the toe, along the surface, helps"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.0,
      "end": 32.77,
      "text": "support the grip."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.46,
      "end": 35.87,
      "text": "To release, the toe starts curling"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.87,
      "end": 37.06,
      "text": "back at its tip."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.5,
      "end": 39.95,
      "text": "Contact progressively breaks from the tip"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.95,
      "end": 41.65,
      "text": "toward the base, rather than the"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.65,
      "end": 43.31,
      "text": "whole pad lifting at once."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.02,
      "end": 45.76,
      "text": "That toe movement is called"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.76,
      "end": 47.32,
      "text": "digital hyperextension."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.95,
      "end": 49.52,
      "text": "Don't confuse it with the angles"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.52,
      "end": 51.42,
      "text": "of the microscopic hairs beneath it."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.19,
      "end": 54.23,
      "text": "So a gecko doesn't simply yank"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.23,
      "end": 55.29,
      "text": "its foot off the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.82,
      "end": 58.21,
      "text": "Close contact, the direction of loading,"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.21,
      "end": 60.96,
      "text": "and controlled toe movement work together"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.96,
      "end": 62.85,
      "text": "to make gripping, and letting go,"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.85,
      "end": 63.4,
      "text": "possible."
    }
  ]
}
